            <div class="container" style="padding-left:2%;max-width:100%">
                <div class="row">

                    <div class="col-md-12">

                        <div class="shadow-lg p-3 mb-5 bg-body rounded" style="padding-left:2%;margin-top:2% ;max-width:100%">


                            <h5 style="color:orange">Course Highlights</h5>
                            <div class="mb-3 mt-2" style="padding-left:2%">
                                An Oracle SQL and PL/SQL course syllabus is typically divided into two core phases: fundamental data management (SQL) and procedural programming (PL/SQL)
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3 mt-2" style="padding-left:2%">

                                <ul>

                                    <li>

                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Oracle SQL Fundamentals</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Introduction</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Database concepts (DBMS, RDBMS), Oracle Database architecture, and tools like SQL Developer or SQL*Plus.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Data Retrieval</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Writing SELECT statements, using aliases, and restricting/sorting data with WHERE and ORDER BY.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Functions</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Single-Row: Character, Number, Date, and Conversion functions (e.g., TO_CHAR, TO_DATE).
                                                    </p>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Aggregate: SUM, AVG, COUNT with GROUP BY and HAVING clauses.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Data Joins</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Retrieving data from multiple tables using Inner, Outer (Left, Right, Full), and Self Joins.
                                                    </p>
                                                 </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Subqueries</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Single-row, multi-row, and correlated subqueries.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Data Manipulation (DML)</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, and MERGE operations, including transaction control (COMMIT, ROLLBACK, SAVEPOINT).
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Schema Objects (DDL)</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        : Creating and managing tables, constraints (Primary/Foreign Key), Views, Indexes, Sequences, and Synonyms.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </div>

                                    </li>
                                    <li>

                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Oracle PL/SQL Programming</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>PL/SQL Basics</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Block structure (Anonymous blocks), variables, constants, and data types.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Control Structures</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Conditional logic (IF-THEN-ELSE, CASE) and iterative loops (FOR, WHILE, Simple Loop).
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Cursor Management</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Implicit and Explicit cursors, cursor attributes, and Cursors with Parameters.
                                                    </p>
                                                    
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Exception Handling</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Trapping predefined Oracle errors and defining custom exceptions.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Subqueries</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Single-row, multi-row, and correlated subqueries.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Stored Subprograms</b>
                                                    <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        <b>Procedures & Functions</b>
                                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                            Creating, executing, and passing parameters (IN, OUT, IN OUT).
                                                        </p>
                                                        <b>Packages</b>
                                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                            Grouping related subprograms into specification and body.
                                                        </p>
                                                    </div>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Database Triggers</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        DML and DDL triggers, Row-level vs. Statement-level firing.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Advanced Topics</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Collections (Nested Tables, Varrays), Dynamic SQL, and Performance Tuning (Bulk Collect, Forall)
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </div>

                                    </li>
                                    
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>



                        <div class="shadow-lg p-3 mb-5 bg-body rounded" style="padding-left:2%;margin-top:2% ;max-width:100%">

                            <h5 style="color:orange">
                                Who can do?
                            </h5>
                            <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                Oracle SQL and PL/SQL training is highly accessible, making it a popular choice for both tech-heavy roles and business-focused positions.

                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3" style="padding-left:2%">
                                <ul>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Students & Freshers</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Essential for those preparing for campus placements and technical internships at top-tier tech companies.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Software Developers</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Engineers currently using Java, Python, or .NET who need to build and manage the backend database of their applications.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Data Professionals</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Aspiring Data Analysts, Data Engineers, and BI Developers who need to extract and manipulate large datasets.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Manual Testers</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Quality Assurance professionals looking to transition into Automation Testing or Database Testing.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Career Switchers</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Professionals from non-technical backgrounds (like Finance, Banking, or Sales) who want to enter the tech sector via data management.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            @Html.Partial("~/Views/Shared/Feedbacks.cshtml")
        </div>
